    "Lastname": "Patterson",
    "countyid": "f5214cb2-953e-41a9-a4ad-71341501e2ad",
    "Firstname": "Kelly",
    "Narrative": "<p>Reporter: Kelly Patterson-443-481-1209</p><p>AAMC</p><p>2001 Medical Parkway</p><p>Annapolis, MD 21401</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>****Note: Written email is uploaded in the documents section of this referral****</strong></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Dad: David W. Ferguson (D.O.B. 11/11/80) (Male, White/Caucasian)-443-477-5093</p><p>1087 Poplar Tree Drive</p><p>Annapolis, MD 21409 (According to MVA)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Grandmother here from FL/brought child to the ER:&nbsp;Kathy Green-410-490-3508</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Child is homeless in AA County with Dad/Bouncing around</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Child:&nbsp;Noah J. Ferguson (D.O.B. 5/22/05) (Male, Caucasian/White)</p><p>(Alias Noah Barnes)</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Family bounces around in hotels in AA County</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Report:</p><p>Reporter states Noah was brought in last night by Ms. Green due to domestic issues/arguments within the family.&nbsp;Dad is on heroin and is regularly using according to Noah.&nbsp;Noah has had to revive his dad via CPR one more than one occasion.&nbsp;Noah is not allowed to leave his dad’s side in case dad overdoses.&nbsp;Child is not really eating and is not enrolled in school.&nbsp;Child is not allowed to interact with peers.&nbsp;He presents as a very parentified, logical, and responsible child.&nbsp;Child has no real support.&nbsp;Grandmother came in town to assist the family with moving from a previous place from which they were evicted.&nbsp;The grandmother will likely be in town for a couple more days.&nbsp;Child reports mom has always been abusive and there is no contact.&nbsp;The family has been staying with Ms. Green’s work colleague for a few days. It does not seem that Noah knows much about Grandmom.&nbsp;Screener requested that reporter attempt to obtain additional information about dad, contact number and address prior to forwarding the written referral.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>2 different Noah Ferguson’s in CIS with same DOB different middle initial</p><p><br></p><p>SN: Screener was advised by Screening supervisor D. Morgan to contact the grandmother to obtain additional information about the family without disclosure of the reporting source.</p><p>SN: Screener attempted to contact Ms. Kathy Green but the call went to voice-mail</p><p>SN: 7/7/2021-Screener contacted and spoke with Kathy Green. She reports that Noah is still at AAMC and their is a meeting scheduled at noon to determine recommendations. Ms. Green states she is visiting the family from Florida and will be here until the oldest child is released from University of MD in Baltimore resulting from a car accident. Ms. Green said she then intends to take the family to Florida with her. Ms. Green also mentioned that there is family support on the Eastern Shore of MD. Screener explained that the purpose of the call is to obtain additional information in order to provide services to the family based on a referral the agency received. Ms. Green said the family is currently residing with one of her colleagues. Despite several attempts to explain why the address is needed Ms. Green declined to provide this information stating she does not want her colleague involved. Ms. Green however, did provide a phone number for Mr. Ferguson (443-477-5093).</p><p>SN: Screener spoke w/ Debbie Morgan AAMC-no address other than the grandmother''s address Florida. Debbie called and spoke with Ginger this AM and advised the Pediatrician (Dr. Fitzpatrick) has concerns about discharging the child and wanted to know who/if there is an assigned CPS worker.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><br></p><p>Assign IRN2 same day to Saperstein</p>",
